PackageReference.NET CLIPackage Manager <pre><code>&lt;ItemGroup&gt;
    &lt;PackageReference Include="Imposter" Version="*" PrivateAssets="all" /&gt;
&lt;/ItemGroup&gt;
</code></pre> <pre><code>dotnet add package Imposter
</code></pre> <pre><code>Install-Package Imposter
</code></pre> <p>This package includes both the source generator (analyzer) and the runtime abstractions.</p> <p>Pro tip</p> <p>To inspect generated sources locally, set <code>EmitCompilerGeneratedFiles</code> and <code>CompilerGeneratedFilesOutputPath</code> in your project. Remove these before committing. <pre><code>&lt;!-- Source code generation settings--&gt;
&lt;PropertyGroup&gt;
    &lt;EmitCompilerGeneratedFiles&gt;true&lt;/EmitCompilerGeneratedFiles&gt;
    &lt;CompilerGeneratedFilesOutputPath&gt;GeneratedFiles&lt;/CompilerGeneratedFilesOutputPath&gt;
&lt;/PropertyGroup&gt;

&lt;!-- Include but don't compile generated code. The system will already compile the code, but this will make it visible for reference.--&gt;
&lt;ItemGroup&gt;
    &lt;Compile Remove="GeneratedFiles\**"/&gt;
    &lt;None Include="GeneratedFiles\**"/&gt;
&lt;/ItemGroup&gt;
</code></pre></p> <p>Pro tip</p> <p>To see what the generator does, set the <code>IMPOSTER_LOG</code> property to <code>true</code> in the project file, on the command line or as an environment variable. The generator then logs the language version, whether it generates the static <code>Imposter()</code> extensions, and each generated imposter with its file name. The log lines are <code>IMPLOG001</code> messages, which <code>dotnet build</code> shows only at detailed verbosity. <pre><code>dotnet build -v:d -p:IMPOSTER_LOG=true
</code></pre></p>
